        "heading": "The Three Doors, as a Decision Path",
        "content": "Framing the shift-long grind of triage as three doors is useful in theory, but the diagram makes the actual decision loop concrete: every alert routes back through the same question — do I have enough evidence right now to walk through close or escalate, or do I genuinely not know yet? The loop back from dig deeper is deliberate: it is not a fourth door, it is a detour that always has to return to the same question, on a timebox, until it resolves into one of the other two. An analyst who cannot point to which arrow they are currently following is the analyst who has quietly stopped making a decision at all.",
